{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/295403-canopic-jar-questions","id":295403,"title":"Canopic Jar Questions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-28T17:23:01-07:00","id":295403,"title":"Canopic Jar Questions","content":"For the first time so far in my RP group, canopic jars have been coming up. I realized I still have some questions regarding both the aftermath and the optionality of their use for resurrection. <br /> <br /> Question one: Can a mummy use a jar for resurrection if her khat is intact? The tone of the sidebar seems to indicate that resurrection from a jar is a sort of last resort before Second Arising. Can the jars be used in other circumstances? For example, can a mummy have her cult resurrect her from a canopic jar to more easily travel between continents or to manage multinational cults? Or do the canopic jars only work after the khat is destroyed, or destroy the khat if used? <br /> <br /> Question two: When the Mummy is deestroyed, does it leave behind a new khat, or the canopic jar? this may itself answer question one; if the jar organ is replaced by the full khat, its used up, and &quot;canopic jar jumping&quot; would be useless as each such teleport would use up an organ.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-28T18:11:29-07:00","id":295468,"title":"","content":"I think the book is reasonably clear on each question. For question one, a Mummy can always choose to resurrect around an organ. The example given of a Mummy whose khat is imprisoned doesn't indicate that the Arisen must first utterly destroy their khat before they resurrect at an organ. He just needs to do enough damage to kill himself.<br /> <br /> As for question two, nothing in the write-up suggests that a Mummy's organs become a new khat. Instead, the sahu forms around the organ, but the organ itself is utterly unchanged by this. Should the sahu be destroyed, the organ will remain behind.<br /> <br /> So yes, a Mummy can &quot;teleport&quot; by having a cultist summon him/herself with an organ rather than the khat. In fact, that's more or less explicitly what the organs are for. They just need to die or finish their descend in order to do it, so doing it mid-descent costs Sekhem and leads to a lot of aggravated damage, and doing it between descents drains a relic or vestige, perhaps permanently. Steep prices either way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}